I decided that implementing comments into GraphXTheatre files before doing another release would be a good idea, but while implementing it I noticed that the way I handle key/value pairs while parsing the file isn't very good. Mainly because they're two separate vectors and aren't directly linked, so if a user comments out a value but not a key, the two vectors will be de-synced. This isn't very good, but due to how I parse all the keys before moving on to the values, I don't know how simple it would be to change this. Let's list the pros and cons.
Pros:
  - Parser is less succeptible to key/value "desync"
    - This also means that forgetting to give a variable a value won't result in a crash or other problems

Cons:
  - Unknown complexity and time cost

