Okay some notes: I forgot that you need to pre-allocate the buffer store for a VBO (or any buffer, actually) and that means either allocating exactly enough data for one object, or specifying a maximum amount of data and making a new buffer when that max is hit. That second option would be nice, but with how the codebase and my skill leveel are, currently, the first option seems best. This means, yes, generating new VBOs for each object (which is less efficient but not by that much form what I've read), but still splitting up vertex attributes. This would just be going back to how things were, however, so I might take a chance on the idea of making big buffers and using them until they're filled and making another buffer. I wanna try that, actually. Okay, I will.

