Ok, so I think it was because of the buffer, ironically; basically, I never destroyed the buffered Theatre, and while that's fine for my code (because only Actors in the current Theatre are ticked), the Jolt objects are still being processed, hence the issues. I solved this by adding a `swapBuffer` function to the Theatre handler which swaps the buffer index and then deletes the old Theatre.

Yeah, now the only crash seems to be from AddressSanitizer when I exit the program (and it's most likely due to the memory leaks LMFAO).